   "mechanism": "TREM2/DAP12 signaling engages PLCG2-dependent phosphoinositide signaling, while INPP5D provides an inhibitory phosphatase arm; the balance determines whether microglia compact amyloid plaques and preserve nearby synapses. Alzheimer risk should rise when this response is too weak or mistimed, consistent with high-risk TREM2 variants and a protective PLCG2 allele, although the protective INPP5D locus does not by itself establish whether lower or context-specific INPP5D activity is beneficial.",
